{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/study-planner","name":"study-planner","description":"AI breaks your syllabus into topics; a spaced-repetition scheduler turns them into a realistic study calendar you can export to Google or Apple Calendar.","category":"Business","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T03:59:56Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:50:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/study-planner/","topics":["github-pages","icalendar","javascript","scheduling","spaced-repetition"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/study-planner/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.411Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.411Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.411Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.411Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI breaks your syllabus into topics; a spaced-repetition scheduler turns them into a realistic study calendar you can export to Google or Apple Calendar.","Enter your exams (date, difficulty, how confident you feel, optional syllabus) and your free hours per weekday. The AI splits each subject into topics with study-hour estimates and tips. A constraint-based scheduler then fills your calendar day by day, ranking sessions by urgency (slack until deadline) × weight (difficulty × lack of confidence). It interleaves subjects, unlocks spaced reviews 2 and 6 days after you finish a topic, and reserves a mock exam and final review before each test. If you don't have enough time, it tells you exactly how many hours you're short."],"features":["Exam editor with difficulty/confidence sliders and optional syllabus","AI topic breakdown with hour estimates and study tips (editable)","Greedy constraint scheduler: urgency × weight priority, subject interleaving, sequential learning units","Spaced repetition: automatic reviews at +2 and +6 days, mock exam and final review before each test","Capacity, days off and overflow warnings with hour shortfall per subject"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/study-planner/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"65fa78887e1401976588275ee8a0aa419c9d782edc64850646a3a7138b9a5d11","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.477Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.477Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"AI breaks your syllabus into topics; a spaced-repetition scheduler turns them into a realistic study calendar you can export to Google or Apple Calendar.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/study-planner/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"index.html is the public home page, login.html handles accounts and app.html is the app.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/study-planner/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"65fa78887e1401976588275ee8a0aa419c9d782edc64850646a3a7138b9a5d11","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/study-planner/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.477Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T03:50:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/study-planner/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.478Z","hash":"65fa78887e1401976588275ee8a0aa419c9d782edc64850646a3a7138b9a5d11","originalBytes":5322,"storedBytes":5322,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["page","src","app","calendar","exam","lib","per","sessions","tests","days","scheduler","settings","today","browser","each","every","focus","runs","study","subject","syllabus","topic","accounts","brief","core.js","difficulty","estimates","functions","generated","grade","grades","hour","how","index.html","provider","pure","readiness","spaced","styles","topics","unit","app.html","bash","before","box","build","calls","capacity","click-to-complete","completed","confidence","constraint","covered","daily","date","day","dom","export","final","groq","home","hours","